# Overprotect says "target creature you control": Bot2's Ornithopter is refused (the refusal) beside Bot1's own (the positive
# control). In response to Bot2's Lightning Bolt on Bot1's Ornithopter (0/2), Overprotect gives it hexproof, so the Bolt has no
# legal target when it resolves and is countered (CR 608.2b): the Ornithopter takes no damage and lives.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Overprotect
Ornithopter
Plains x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Ornithopter
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Overprotect.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Hand.Overprotect.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Damage = 0

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 5
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
